TARGET: lib/tree-check.js
REASON: Upstream swaps the export for the checking implementation by assigning
to `module.exports` from inside the debug callback.  `module` does not exist in
an ES module, so under ESM that assignment raises a ReferenceError the moment
the module is imported with debug active, and the checking implementation is
never reachable otherwise.  Selecting the implementation through a binding the
default export closes over keeps both arms working: the identity function
normally, the full tree check when debug is on.

---
SEARCH:
// should only ever run this check in debug mode
export default (tree) => tree;
debug(() => (module.exports = checkTree));
REPLACE:
// should only ever run this check in debug mode
let selected = (tree) => tree;
debug(() => {
  selected = checkTree;
});

export default (tree, checkUnreachable) => selected(tree, checkUnreachable);
